# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-15), from the product owner's decision in collab/QUESTIONS.md (Q16: at a start a waiting place keeps its room); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: a browser, an editor and a mail window are docked side by side, the notes float. In the evening the Mac is shut down. In the
# morning Arbor is up at the login long before the apps, and they bring their windows back one after the other, the one in the middle first.
# Nobody moves twice because somebody else is late: whoever comes goes straight to the place it had, and a hole waits for the others.
# A restart of the Mac is: Arbor quits, every window closes, Arbor starts, and `open` brings the windows back under new numbers.
# Reference: T60, issue #3 rule 3 (a window moves once, to where it ends up).
display-size 2560x1440
open Browser 1000x700
open Editor 900x700
open Mail 800x600
open Notes 200x150
title 101 News
title 102 Draft
title 103 Inbox
dock 101 left
dock 102 beside 101 right
dock 103 beside 102 right
balance all
expect left-of 101 102
expect left-of 102 103
expect at 102 861 37
expect size 102 838x1391
relaunch quit
close 101
close 102
close 103
close 104
relaunch start
expect ok
status
expect replied 3 places kept for windows that are not open yet
# The editor is first. It takes the place in the middle at once, with room on both sides for who is still to come.
open Editor 900x700
expect moved-once
expect docked 105
expect at 105 861 37
expect size 105 838x1391
title 105 Draft
expect still
# Looking around changes nothing: there and back, and the holes are still kept.
zoom 105
show-all
expect at 105 861 37
expect size 105 838x1391
# The mail window comes, then the browser. Whoever is there already stays where it is.
open Mail 800x600
expect moved-once
expect still 105
expect docked 106
expect left-of 105 106
title 106 Inbox
open Browser 1000x700
expect moved-once
expect still 105
expect still 106
expect docked 107
expect left-of 107 105
title 107 News
expect size 105 838x1391
expect size 106 837x1391
expect size 107 837x1391
status
expect ok

# Another morning, and the browser does not come. For three minutes its place is kept, and when they are over nothing moves by itself.
relaunch quit
close 105
close 106
close 107
relaunch start
open Editor 900x700
title 108 Draft
open Mail 800x600
expect still 108
title 109 Inbox
wait 400
expect still
expect at 108 861 37
status
expect replied 1 place kept
# The room goes back with the next layout that the person causes.
relayout
expect moved-once
expect at 108 12 37
status
expect ok

# A third morning: whoever changes the arrangement meanwhile has taken it in hand, and the hole closes in the same move.
relaunch quit
close 108
close 109
relaunch start
open Mail 800x600
title 110 Inbox
open Notes 200x150
expect still 110
dock 111 right
expect moved-once
expect docked 111
expect at 110 12 37
# The editor's place still waits, without room, as a minimized window's does.
status
expect replied 1 place kept
open Editor 900x700
title 112 Draft
expect docked 112
expect left-of 112 110
